    ],
    "Description": "In Apache Airflow before 3.3.0, the REST API task-instance detail and list endpoints returned a deferred task's trigger kwargs without masking. When a deferred operator passed a secret (for example a provider API key) into its trigger, any authenticated user with DAG-scoped task-instance read access for that DAG could read that secret in clear text while the task was deferred.\nUsers should upgrade to apache-airflow 3.3.0 or later, which masks sensitive values in trigger kwargs returned by the API.",
    "Origin": "UNSPECIFIED",
    "PublishedAt": "2026-07-07T12:31:36Z",
    "Severity": "MODERATE",
    "Summary": "Apache Airflow exposes deferred trigger kwargs in task-instance API responses",
    "UpdatedAt": "2026-09-04T19:28:50Z",
